---
// MetroClusteringExhibit.astro - Unsupervised Operating Mode Clusters & Failure Concentration
const clusterModes = [
  { name: 'Idle', share: 67.5, failureWindows: 7, totalWindows: 34096, failShare: 0.7, desc: 'Lowest APU pressure and minimal motor draw' },
  { name: 'Start/Stop Cycling', share: 26.45, failureWindows: 0, totalWindows: 13361, failShare: 0.0, desc: 'Normal intermittent compressor operation' },
  { name: 'Sustained High Load', share: 6.05, failureWindows: 985, totalWindows: 3056, failShare: 99.3, desc: 'Highest continuous motor current and air throughput' }
];
---

<div class="exhibit-wrapper" id="metro-clustering-exhibit">
  <div class="exhibit-header">
    <div>
      <span class="exhibit-tag font-mono">EXHIBIT 5.1: CLUSTER SEPARATION &amp; ANOMALY OVERLAP</span>
      <h3 class="exhibit-title">K-Means Sensor Mode Partitioning (50,513 5-Minute Windows)</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="font-mono text-xs status-note">
      <a href="https://metropt3-clustering.streamlit.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="live-pill">
        <span class="status-dot deployed"></span> View Live Streamlit App ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sr-only">
    Clustering evaluation of 50,513 five-minute sensor windows on the MetroPT-3 compressor dataset. Sustained High Load mode represents only 6.05% of all operating time, yet captures 985 of the 992 total failure windows (99.3%).
  </div>

  <!-- Cluster Mode Distribution Bars -->
  <div class="clusters-grid font-mono">
    {clusterModes.map(c => (
      <div class={`cluster-card ${c.share === 6.05 ? 'highlight-cluster' : ''}`}>
        <div class="cluster-top">
          <span class="c-name">{c.name}</span>
          <span class="c-share">{c.share}% of Time</span>
        </div>
        
        <p class="c-desc">{c.desc}</p>

        <div class="cluster-stat-row">
          <span class="c-lbl">Total Windows:</span>
          <span class="c-val">{c.totalWindows.toLocaleString()}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="cluster-stat-row">
          <span class="c-lbl">Failure Windows:</span>
          <span class={`c-val ${c.failureWindows > 0 ? 'alert' : ''}`}>{c.failureWindows} ({c.failShare}%)</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bar-track">
          <div 
            class={`bar-fill ${c.share === 6.05 ? 'fill-alert' : 'fill-norm'}`} 
            style={`width: ${c.share === 6.05 ? 99.3 : (c.share / 70) * 100}%`}
          ></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <!-- Analytical Takeaway Box -->
  <div class="insight-box font-mono">
    <span class="insight-title">KEY METHODOLOGICAL TAKEAWAY &amp; HONEST LIMITATION:</span>
    <p class="insight-body">
      Although <strong>99.3% of all failure windows</strong> concentrate inside the "Sustained High Load" mode (a 16x concentration over baseline), 
      only <strong>32.2% of windows in that mode</strong> represent active failures. Therefore, unsupervised clustering successfully identifies 
      <em>where</em> failures occur physically, but cannot serve as an actionable predictive alarm without pre-failure lead-time labeling.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .exhibit-wrapper {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  .exhibit-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .exhibit-header {
      flex-direction: row;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: flex-end;
    }
  }

  .exhibit-tag {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .exhibit-title {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .status-note {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .live-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    color: var(--color-status-deployed);
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .clusters-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .clusters-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .cluster-card {
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .cluster-card.highlight-cluster {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(185, 56, 34, 0.08);
  }

  .cluster-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .c-name {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .c-share {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .c-desc {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
    min-height: 32px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .cluster-stat-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .c-lbl {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .c-val {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .c-val.alert {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .bar-track {
    width: 100%;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .bar-fill.fill-norm {
    background-color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .bar-fill.fill-alert {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .insight-box {
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .insight-title {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .insight-body {
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }
</style>
